  "suffix_checkpoint": 450,
  "scope": "Prospective new900row banks disjoint from all1,988,296 IDs in the declared Ripper completion-source ledger. New source, noise, tie and feedbackpermutation seeds. Not globally untouched or externaldistribution evidence; no puzzle-solver inputs.",
  "sampling": "Perbank independently seeded choice900without replacement from all sorted1,843,698eligibleIDs; no calibration split. Crossbank source-ID overlap allowed and reported. Seal all source identities before selected labels. Feedbackpermutations fixed in this protocol before source IDs.",
  "policy": "Greedy pair weights(8/9)^actual_joint_count/(1+feedback_count), exponent1. Aligned feedback is actual past equality matrix; control uses actual past equality matrix[fixed_permutation,fixed_permutation]. Each arm has its own actual observed history. No hard exclusions, calibration or suppliednoiseprobabilities. Both use H1ba/H1bb tie permutations. Final recovery always uses true-coordinate observed counts.",
  "predictability": "At eachrow hash prior actual joint/equality state, compute/finalize mask using only thatstate/tieorder/frozenfeedbackpermutation, then access current source/noiselatent. Immutable-state checks and independent sequential mask/noise/state replay. Alter sources+noise only atrows>=450 and rerun; first450 masks/labels/counts must remain identical.",
  "primary": "Endpoint1 procedure: aligned>=29/32 certified integral exact. Success bounds S_aligned to S_aligned+U_aligned. Supported if lower>=29; falsified if upper<29; otherwise inconclusive.",
  "alignment_endpoint": "Endpoint2 finite alignment advantage: aligned-minus-permuted exact-bank count>=4/32. Lower=S_aligned-(S_permuted+U_permuted); upper=S_aligned+U_aligned-S_permuted. Supported if lower>=4; falsified if upper<4; otherwise inconclusive. Report endpoints separately, no combined success claim.",
  "mechanism_limit": "Cellpermutation changes feedback location and trajectory, including exposure/magnitude pathways. Endpoint2 is a procedure-level alignment intervention, not proof of a unique causal mediator. Endpoint1 alone establishes no alignment mechanism. No posthoc exponent/mask tuning.",
  "noise": "Each bank,row has new independent U and uniform81positionpermutation; corruptwholeboard iffU<9/160. Identical underlying noisyboard shared across aligned/permuted arms; eachhas own pastobservedhistory. Noise RNG neverdepends on masks. No calibration collected.",
  "recovery": "Unchanged all3240-pair Laplace-rate degree20 LP and same-arm top810controls. No archivedsame-source comparator or extraLPs. Fractional returnedoptimum resolvedfailure, not proof no integralcooptimum; no snapping/uniqueness claim.",
  "supplied_prior": "Exactly 20 incident retained edges per cell, implying exactly 810 undirected edges. The top810 control receives that cardinality directly. These are explicit structural priors; no prior-free or uniqueness claim.",
  "cost": "Integer round-half-even(1000000*(c+1)/(m+2)). Exact integer quotient/remainder producer; independent Fraction rounding auditor. Laplace-smoothed empirical equality rate; no supplied q0 or q1, no tuning. Unexposed pair cost500000.",
  "certificate": "No primal rounding/snapping. Literal primal values must belong to {0,0.5,1}. Multiply by two exactly; require exact degree40. Reconstruct node dual y2=round-to-nearest-even(2*y_float), requiring absolute reconstruction error<=1e-6. Set upper dual z2=min(0,2*w-y2_i-y2_j). Check integer dual feasibility, both complementarity conditions and exact equality sum(w*x2)=20*sum(y2)+sum(z2). Costs and duals restricted to absolute value<2^48. No alternate denominators or fallback scheme.",
